// "[subject] draws N" ([CR#121.1]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT draw — that player
// draws N cards, ONE AT A TIME ([CR#121.2] — a per-card SEQUENCE, NOT a
// simultaneous batch like mill). `Draws` is `Draw`'s twin: a `Batch(N, ...)`
// over the per-unit `By(who, Draw)`. The engine runs the N contained draws
// SEQUENTIALLY, each binding the library top LATE and empty-checking BEFORE its
// move, so an empty library loses the game ([CR#121.4,104.3c]).
//
// NOT a keyword action ([CR#701] does not list drawing — it is [CR#121]) and NOT
// a `Composite`: drawing is irreducible ([CR#121.5]), so there is no body. See
// `Draw.ron` for the full note, including why the `KeywordAction` macro kind
// stays (it is the English verb registry, not a CR claim).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) is `By`'s agent — a real slot, not a coordinate scraped off a
// body selection. The template renders the subject context-aware ("Target player
// draws two cards.", "Each player draws a card."); the count spells its noun via
// the `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Draws(It, 1) (the announced player target / Each-bound player, Jace
// Beleren) / Draws(Target(0), 2).
(
    name: "Draws",
    template: "${0} draws ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    // Two frames: the corpus alternation this macro's own doc comment
    // motivates (`docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
    // corpus-alternation.md` §3/§6 — gain/lose are stable `you`-declarative,
    // but `draw` alternates, and imperative "Draw" so dominates the
    // `Param(0) = You` case that a guarded frame reproducing `Draw`'s own
    // wording is the natural default). The guarded frame pre-binds param 0
    // (`Reference`) to `You` and holes only param 1 (`Count`); the unguarded
    // frame spells the subject out for every other filler. Both are excepted
    // from G2 like `Draw.ron` (checked-in template uses the `card|cards`
    // codec).
    frames: [
        (text: "draw <Param(1)> cards", when: [(0, "You")], position: Main),
        "<Param(0)> draws <Param(1)> cards",
    ],
    body: Batch(Param(1), By(Param(0), DrawCard)),
)
